From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jhansi kotipalli <jkotipal@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] libsync: use a constant atomic initializer

GCC 15 no longer exposes ATOMIC_VAR_INIT in the C mode used by this recipe.
An atomic integer can be statically initialized from the same constant value.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform-specific toolchain compatibility]
Signed-off-by: jkotipal <jkotipal@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 sync.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sync.c b/sync.c
--- a/sync.c
+++ b/sync.c
@@ -95,5 +95,5 @@ enum uapi_version {
     UAPI_LEGACY
 };
-static atomic_int g_uapi_version = ATOMIC_VAR_INIT(UAPI_UNKNOWN);
+static atomic_int g_uapi_version = UAPI_UNKNOWN;
 
 // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
